Z||000000||fierospeeder||11-22-2000||07:52 PM||||Anyone in here use the free juno service?<P>I do, and i think its december 2 or 4, that juno wants to cut our unlimited service, and or add more advertisements on our screen.<P>They dont really know what they are going to do yet, but they have some ideas.  Juno cant afford to pay the cost now for free juno.<P>I would think they would stop new "free juno users" from signing up, instead of what they have planned.<P>It seems bogus, and same with aol.  I use to own aol, but i still can get on with my girlfriends account so im not worried.<P>Aol is still 19 bucks?  They have ton of advertisements on their service which is so annoying.  Aol also is suppose to provide fast speed hookup? i can get 44,000 with juno easier then aol and all of them use the same dial up networks around me.||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||11-23-2000||10:25 AM||||You're witnessing the death of free Internet service...it wasn't that long ago that everyone thought free was the way of the future and AOL was doomed.<P>But every free service has failed to reach profitability. Companies like Juno and CMGI that provide free service are in dire financial condition.<P>I really don't have a problem with Juno charging $9.95 if it gets rid of the pop-up ads. Their service is by far the best of the free/low cost services.||||reg||1
